{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"171.159.64.10","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":76602,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7561c384b75ec4220e0a1066f58d98fc","RawContent":"[quote name=\"yogahhh\" post=\"1878671\" timestamp=\"1416351172\"]\nIm getting married April 9th at Sandals Grande Rivieria!!!\nWe are just inviting parents, so I think we will just venture to one of the many onsite restuarants for dinner after the 30 minute reception. Honestly, not blown away by the seated dinner options, and just find it silly to spend the extra $$ when we are at an AI! I also like that it will give our parents an option to choose their own dinner\nHas anyone else done this? Suggestions on which restuarant? Im leaning towards Bayside or Reef Terrance.[\/quote]I agree with you. I did my wedding at Sandals  Whitehouse  on June 7,2014. I went with free hot and cold horsey divers..(lol), added additonal 30 min to  and did dj for music. My ceremony was at 4pm and we took pictures after, while everyone was having signature cocatails, etc. Then we started reception, after reception we all chose restaurant and went and ate together, that way people could choose whatever they wanted and as much as they wanted. was awesome.","Attachments":[],"Id":1882384,"PostDate":1420828578,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>yogahhh, on 18 November 2014 - 03:52 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Im getting married April 9th at Sandals Grande Rivieria!!!<\/p>\n<p>We are just inviting parents, so I think we will just venture to one of the many onsite restuarants for dinner after the 30 minute reception. Honestly, not blown away by the seated dinner options, and just find it silly to spend the extra $$ when we are at an AI! I also like that it will give our parents an option to choose their own dinner<\/p>\n<p>Has anyone else done this? Suggestions on which restuarant? Im leaning towards Bayside or Reef Terrance.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>I agree with you. I did my wedding at Sandals\u00a0 Whitehouse\u00a0 on June 7,2014. I went with free hot and cold\u00a0horsey divers..(lol), added additonal 30 min to\u00a0 and did dj for music. My ceremony was at 4pm and we took pictures after, while everyone was having signature cocatails, etc. Then we started reception, after reception we all chose restaurant and went and ate together, that way people could choose whatever they wanted and as much as they wanted. was awesome.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"shugapop12@aol.com","IpAddress":"66.87.100.226","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1369920425,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-270119.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"shugapop1","Id":270119,"Name":"shugapop1","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":11,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
